# The Workspace image's build context is the repo root (docker/workspace/Dockerfile, brief 102 task 12).
# BuildKit reads this file, and not the root .dockerignore, because it sits beside that Dockerfile
# under the Dockerfile's own name: the sync image's allow-list (the root file) is not touched.
#
# An allow-list: only the three folders that Dockerfile copies from are sent. Every node_modules,
# dist and coverage folder and every .env file stay out, so nothing host-built (a Windows
# node_modules has the wrong native binaries) and nothing secret reaches a layer. The pinned CA
# does not come from this context: compose.yaml hands its folder to the build as the
# named context `harness-certs`.
*
!docker/workspace/
!workspace/
!mcp-server/
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/.env
**/.env.*
